        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0412" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.516/600: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-20T14:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Your 323, May 10, 5 p.m. Please inform the Chinese Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs orally and informally and in confidence that the Department has
                    communicated to representatives of the American banks in Shanghai its views
                    that, while we recognize that American banks have responsibilities of their own
                    and have to protect their own interests, the Department would welcome the
                    maintenance by foreign banks in China of a united front in refraining from
                    action which might assist toward establishing the new bank and launching the new
                    currency.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai and Peiping. Shanghai please mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
